- A tutorial packaged according to the format passes the format's validation\n  pass (manifest checks complete and pass) without any Dashboard release\n  being involved.\n- The format is reviewed and agreed by the teams that consume it: the\n  Dashboard gallery implementers and the tutorial authors for both notebook\n  and pipeline tutorials.\n- Packaging an example tutorial per the format is demonstrated end to end\n  (metadata present, images pinned, validation manifest passes).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P1)**: \"A tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images,\n  validation manifest) is defined so tutorials are versioned and testable\n  independently of Dashboard releases.\" This epic is the direct\n  implementation of HLR-3. Note: the epic's priority is P0 by priority\n  inheritance — the packaging format is the prerequisite artifact that the P0\n  gallery and P0 tutorial work build against, while the HLR itself is\n  labeled P1 in the strategy.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46098,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a00f47e42199fa7","agent_id":"a9c35f164d8e7c9cb","session_id":"ef27924f-e37d-4918-8e80-2a9c242f8803","uuid":"ec17dbcf-d9ac-4a6b-9ff2-7433daa6103d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:25:58.544Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9019"}
