er's project with the tutorial notebook loaded, using the tutorial's\n  pinned images.\n- Launching a pipeline tutorial from the gallery imports the pipeline into\n  the user's project and the imported pipeline is visible in the project's\n  pipeline view (this validates the Data Science Pipelines integration — no\n  pipeline platform code changes are in scope for this epic).\n- End-to-end launch of at least one packaged tutorial of each kind (workbench\n  notebook and imported pipeline) is verified against the current release.\n- The gallery can be disabled through the Dashboard's existing configuration\n  mechanism.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)**: \"The Dashboard has a tutorial gallery from which a user can\n  launch a tutorial into their project (opening a workbench with the\n  notebook, or importing the pipeline).\" This epic is the direct\n  implementation of HLR-1, covering both launch modes.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46098,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a00f47e42199fa7","agent_id":"a9c35f164d8e7c9cb","session_id":"ef27924f-e37d-4918-8e80-2a9c242f8803","uuid":"728f56b0-548b-44af-a8ac-c5634e0c6e98","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:26:05.293Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9019"}
