 Dashboard release.\n51\t- Define versioning rules so a tutorial can be updated and re-tested\n52\t  independently of Dashboard release cadence.\n53\t- Document the format for the teams that author tutorials and build the\n54\t  gallery.\n55\t\n56\tThe scope stays at the format level: concrete schema field names, storage\n57\tlocation, and tooling implementation choices are decisions for the\n58\timplementing team.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- A format specification exists covering tutorial metadata, image pinning,\n63\t  and the validation manifest, with versioning rules that allow a tutorial to\n64\t  be updated without a Dashboard release.\n65\t- A tutorial packaged according to the format passes the format's validation\n66\t  pass (manifest checks complete and pass) without any Dashboard release\n67\t  being involved.\n68\t- The format is reviewed and agreed by the teams that consume it: the\n69\t  Dashboard gallery implementers and the tutorial authors for both notebook\n70\t  and pipeline tutorials.\n71\t- Packaging an example tutorial per the format is demonstrated end to end\n72\t  (metadata present, images pinned, validation manifest passes).\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: \"A tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images,\n77\t  validation manifest) is defined so tutorials are versioned and testable\n78\t  independently of Dashboard releases.\" This epic is the direct\n79\t  implementation of HLR-3. Note: the epic's priority is P0 by priority\n80\t  inheritance — the packaging format is the prerequisite artifact that the P0\n81\t  gallery and P0 tutorial work build against, while the HLR itself is\n82\t  labeled P1 in the strategy.\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0a08780acc46808","agent_id":"ab4064dbdda028e0c","session_id":"ef27924f-e37d-4918-8e80-2a9c242f8803","uuid":"46cf782b-da82-43fa-99f0-ce7a73aa6caa","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:28:02.234Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1933