{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8bbe4b4999cda397","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9019 (Curated getting-started tutorial gallery)\n11\t\n12\t## Strategy Overview\n13\t\n14\tRHAISTRAT-9019 delivers a curated tutorial gallery in the Dashboard: maintained,\n15\ttested tutorials (notebooks and pipelines) that users launch into their own\n16\tproject with one click. The strategy itself names three distinct kinds of work —\n17\tproduct code (gallery and launch mechanics), authored content (the tutorials),\n18\tand documentation — with different owners and review processes. The problem\n19\tstatement's explicit multi-stream structure means the below-threshold triage\n20\tdoes not apply, and the presence of Dashboard product code means this is not a\n21\tdocs-only strategy.\n22\t\n23\tNo Investigation epics were created: the strategy's Open Questions section is\n24\t\"None\", and there are no risks tables, pending reviews, or conditional ADRs.\n25\tThe one design-shaped item, the tutorial packaging format (HLR-3), is a\n26\tdefined deliverable (a spec plus validation manifest), not an open question —\n27\tit becomes an Implementation epic that other epics build against.\n28\t\n29\t## Epic List\n30\t\n31\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n32\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n33\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 |\n34\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Dashboard tutorial gallery with one-click launch into projects | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n35\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 | Curated notebook tutorials for five core onboarding journeys | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 |\n36\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Curated first-pipeline tutorial | Implementation | RHOAI Pipelines | P0 |\n37\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | Tutorial gallery usage and contribution documentation | Implementation | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n38\t\n39\t## Dependency DAG\n40\t\n41\t```mermaid\n42\tgraph TD\n43\t  E001[\"RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 Tutorial packaging format\"] --> E002[\"RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 Dashboard gallery + launch\"]\n44\t  E001 --> E003[\"RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 Notebook tutorials (5 journeys)\"]\n45\t  E001 --> E004[\"RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 Pipeline tutorial\"]\n46\t  E001 --> E005[\"RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 Documentation\"]\n47\t  E002 --> E005\n48\t  E003 --> E005\n49\t  E004 --> E005\n50\t```\n51\t\n52\tCritical path: E001 → E002 → E005 (length 3).\n53\t\n54\t## DAG Justification\n55\t\n56\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n57\t|------|------|-----------|\n58\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 13 (artifact built against) | The gallery code consumes the packaging format's metadata and validation manifest to render and launch tutorials; the format is an API-like artifact the Dashboard builds against, so it must exist first. |\n59\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 12/13 (framework → consumer) | The tutorials are packaged, versioned, and validated per the format; authoring them before the format exists would force repackaging — two epics building the same data structure independently. |\n60\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 12/13 (framework → consumer) | Same as above for the pipeline tutorial: it is authored and validated as a packaged tutorial. |\n61\t| E001, E002, E003, E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | The documentation describes the gallery, the tutorials, and the contribution process built by this strategy; it is blocked by every Implementation epic. These edges do not push priority onto E005 (docs-authoring priority exception). |\n62\t| (no edge) E002 ∥ E003/E004 | Rule 14 (parallel) | The gallery builds against the format, not against specific tutorial content; tutorials are runtime-consumed content, not a build-against artifact. End-to-end launch verification is an acceptance criterion on the gallery epic, not a DAG edge. |\n63\t| (no edge) E003 ∥ E004 | Rule 14 (parallel) | Different teams and components authoring independent content; no shared artifact beyond the format both consume. |\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n66\t\n67\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement | Epic(s) | Notes |\n68\t|-----|----------|-------------|---------|-------|\n69\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Dashboard tutorial gallery with one-click launch (workbench with notebook, or pipeline import) | RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Direct mapping; both launch modes are in scope of the gallery epic. |\n70\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Six curated tutorials covering the core journeys, each tested against the current release | RHAISTRAT-9019-E003, RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Split by epic-boundary rule 1 (different component and team): five notebook-centric journeys (Notebooks / Workbenches) and the first-pipeline journey (Data Science Pipelines / RHOAI Pipelines). Together they cover all six journeys. |\n71\t| HLR-3 | P1 | Tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) for versioned, independently testable tutorials | RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Kept as its own epic (a spec-and-tooling deliverable consumed by three other epics), not merged into the tutorial epics. Its epic priority is P0 by priority inheritance: it is the prerequisite that the P0 gallery and both P0 tutorial epics build against — an epic blocking all P0 work is implicitly P0. The HLR's own P1 label is recorded here. |\n72\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation covers using the gallery and the contribution process | RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | docs-authoring priority exception: derived from the strategy frontmatter priority (Major → P1), not from HLR-4's P2 label; docs epics do not push priority upstream. |\n73\t\n74\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n75\t\n76\t## Health Warnings\n77\t\n78\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n79\t  Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria section, no\n80\t  Non-Functional Requirements, and no Technical Approach / Staff Engineer\n81\t  Input. Decomposition proceeded from the Affected Components list, HLR table,\n82\t  and problem statement. Team assignments were inferred from the\n83\t  architecture-context owning-team fields (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard,\n84\t  Notebooks → Workbenches, Data Science Pipelines → RHOAI Pipelines); no\n85\t  architecture-context file exists for the Documentation component, so the\n86\t  RHOAI Documentation team assignment on E005 is an inference a human should\n87\t  confirm.\n88\t- **Planning note (epic size)**: the notebook-tutorials epic (five authored,\n89\t  packaged, and release-tested tutorials) is above the ~2-week epic-size\n90\t  guideline by scope arithmetic — five substantive pieces of curated content,\n91\t  each individually tested against the current release. Kept as one epic\n92\t  because the five tutorials form a single curated set sharing the packaging\n93\t  format, a consistent style, and one validation/test harness; a split would\n94\t  fragment one curation pass into parallel duplicates of the same packaging\n95\t  and test scaffolding. **Re-split trigger**: re-split this epic if any\n96\t  tutorial's authoring or testing exceeds its per-tutorial estimate, or if\n97\t  review shows the journeys diverge enough to need separate curation passes.\n98\t- **Priority inheritance note**: HLR-3 is P1 but its epic (E001) is P0 because\n99\t  it gates all P0 work in the strategy (gallery + both tutorial epics). This\n100\t  is inheritance, not a priority inversion — recorded in the matrix row above.\n101\t- **Passive component — Data Science Pipelines**: no DSP platform code change\n102\t  is implied by the strategy. Pipeline import is exercised through the\n103\t  existing KFP v2 surface (per the architecture context, pipeline runs are\n104\t  surfaced in the Dashboard and the KFP v2 REST API/SDK is the interface), so\n105\t  DSP validation is an acceptance criterion on the gallery epic; the RHOAI\n106\t  Pipelines team instead owns the pipeline tutorial content epic.\n107\t- **Integration coordination (not a DAG edge)**: the gallery epic's end-to-end\n108\t  acceptance criterion requires at least one packaged tutorial of each kind to\n109\t  exist at verification time. This is a scheduling coordination point between\n110\t  the gallery epic and the tutorial epics, deliberately not a dependency edge\n111\t  (the gallery is developed against the format, and any packaged tutorial can\n112\t  serve as the verification vehicle).\n113\t\n114\t## Component Mapping Notes\n115\t\n116\t- `Notebooks` is the canonical component for both E001 (packaging format) and\n117\t  E003 (notebook tutorials). The format spans notebook and pipeline tutorials;\n118\t  it is assigned the single most-relevant canonical name (tutorials are\n119\t  primarily notebooks; five of six journeys) and the span is noted here.\n120\t- `Data Science Pipelines` maps to E004 (the pipeline tutorial content). The\n121\t  DSP platform itself is passive for code (see Health Warnings).\n122\t- `Documentation` maps to E005 (docs-authoring).\n123\t- All component values are copied verbatim from `.context/rhai-components.txt`.\n124\t\n125\t## Tiered Delivery\n126\t\n127\tNot applicable — there are no external dependencies with uncertain timing;\n128\tall work is internal to the platform teams.\n129\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92d45e8a6514990a","agent_id":"a4b7c8d14bf1c20bd","session_id":"ef27924f-e37d-4918-8e80-2a9c242f8803","uuid":"7588f50f-e0f1-49c8-a99e-4f5be92a3d13","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:32:21.597Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8bbe4b4999cda397","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
