{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9134f2dcdfe8e43c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9019-E001\n3\ttitle: Tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n5\tcomponent: Notebooks\n6\tteam: Workbenches\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: -1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: -1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 0\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 1\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest)\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic defines the tutorial packaging format that makes tutorials versioned\n34\tand testable independently of Dashboard releases. It produces the format\n35\tspecification — tutorial metadata, pinned images, and a validation manifest —\n36\tplus the means to validate a packaged tutorial against that manifest. The\n37\tformat is the shared artifact that the Dashboard tutorial gallery renders and\n38\tlaunches, and that every curated tutorial is authored, packaged, and tested\n39\tagainst.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Define the tutorial metadata model a packaged tutorial carries (identity,\n44\t  journey description, launch hints for both a workbench notebook and an\n45\t  imported pipeline).\n46\t- Define the pinned-image policy for tutorial content so a tutorial always\n47\t  runs against known image versions.\n48\t- Define the validation manifest and the validation pass that checks a\n49\t  packaged tutorial for completeness and correctness without requiring a\n50\t  Dashboard release.\n51\t- Define versioning rules so a tutorial can be updated and re-tested\n52\t  independently of Dashboard release cadence.\n53\t- Document the format for the teams that author tutorials and build the\n54\t  gallery.\n55\t\n56\tThe scope stays at the format level: concrete schema field names, storage\n57\tlocation, and tooling implementation choices are decisions for the\n58\timplementing team.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- A format specification exists covering tutorial metadata, image pinning,\n63\t  and the validation manifest, with versioning rules that allow a tutorial to\n64\t  be updated without a Dashboard release.\n65\t- A tutorial packaged according to the format passes the format's validation\n66\t  pass (manifest checks complete and pass) without any Dashboard release\n67\t  being involved.\n68\t- The format is reviewed and agreed by the teams that consume it: the\n69\t  Dashboard gallery implementers and the tutorial authors for both notebook\n70\t  and pipeline tutorials.\n71\t- Packaging an example tutorial per the format is demonstrated end to end\n72\t  (metadata present, images pinned, validation manifest passes).\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: \"A tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images,\n77\t  validation manifest) is defined so tutorials are versioned and testable\n78\t  independently of Dashboard releases.\" This epic is the direct\n79\t  implementation of HLR-3. Note: the epic's priority is P0 by priority\n80\t  inheritance — the packaging format is the prerequisite artifact that the P0\n81\t  gallery and P0 tutorial work build against, while the HLR itself is\n82\t  labeled P1 in the strategy.\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92d45e8a6514990a","agent_id":"a4b7c8d14bf1c20bd","session_id":"ef27924f-e37d-4918-8e80-2a9c242f8803","uuid":"a4499c7a-8fcd-437f-a3a9-4c0c3a0c83b6","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:32:23.996Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9