data, pinned images, validation\n50\t  manifest) so tutorials are rendered and launched from their packages,\n51\t  versioned independently of Dashboard releases.\n52\t- Gate the gallery through the Dashboard's existing per-component feature\n53\t  configuration so it can be enabled/disabled without code changes.\n54\t- Fold in any captions, labels, or reference updates in the Dashboard that\n55\t  fall out of this change.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A user can open the tutorial gallery from the Dashboard and see the curated\n60\t  tutorials with their metadata.\n61\t- Launching a notebook tutorial from the gallery opens a workbench in the\n62\t  user's project with the tutorial notebook loaded, using the tutorial's\n63\t  pinned images.\n64\t- Launching a pipeline tutorial from the gallery imports the pipeline into\n65\t  the user's project and the imported pipeline is visible in the project's\n66\t  pipeline view (this validates the Data Science Pipelines integration — no\n67\t  pipeline platform code changes are in scope for this epic).\n68\t- End-to-end launch of at least one packaged tutorial of each kind (workbench\n69\t  notebook and imported pipeline) is verified against the current release.\n70\t- The gallery can be disabled through the Dashboard's existing configuration\n71\t  mechanism.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: \"The Dashboard has a tutorial gallery from which a user can\n76\t  launch a tutorial into their project (opening a workbench with the\n77\t  notebook, or importing the pipeline).\" This epic is the direct\n78\t  implementation of HLR-1, covering both launch modes.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92d45e8a6514990a","agent_id":"a4b7c8d14bf1c20bd","session_id":"ef27924f-e37d-4918-8e80-2a9c242f8803","uuid":"b2c73d64-dcad-4b41-a63c-edf512207f4b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:32:24.719Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd5f2ed5287bc3c3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","s